            description: Some("Hot mixing: quicklime is ground and blended dry with volcanic ash, and the water goes in last. The lime slakes in the mix itself, the heat cooks it, and white lumps of lime, lime clasts, are left through the set concrete. Admir Masic's MIT team proposed it in 2023 from a city wall at Privernum, and confirmed it in 2025 at a Pompeii building site that Vesuvius buried mid-job in 79 CE: its dry piles of premixed quicklime and ash were still waiting for water. Vitruvius had written that the lime was slaked into a paste first."),
